ant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOKUYAMA CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, HIROMASA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANAGI, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IBARAGI KAZUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAIRA HIROAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO HIROMASA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YANAGI HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IBARAGI, KAZUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAIRA, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, HIROMASA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANAGI, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A film responsive to anions which is obtained by forming into film either a composition comprising an onium salt compound, e.g., trioctylmethylammonium chloride or tetraoctylammonium bromide, and an aromatic boric diester compound, e.g., a (p-alkyloxy)phenyl borate ester, or a composition which comprises these two ingredients and a film-forming polymer, e.g., poly(vinyl chloride) or polystyrene, and may further contain a lipid-soluble anion salt, e.g., tetraphenyl borate. With this film, an ion-selective electrode is obtained with which hydrogen carbonate ions contained in a body fluid can be rapidly determined with high sensitivity and high selectivity and which has a long life.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un film réceptif aux anions, ce film étant obtenu par formation en film d'une composition comprenant un composé de sel d'onium, par exemple un chlorure de trioctylméthylammonium ou un bromure de tétraoctylammonium et un composé diester borique aromatique, par exemple un ester de borate de (p-alkyloxy)phényle; ou d'une composition comprenant ces deux ingrédients et un polymère filmogène, par exemple un polychlorure de vinyle ou un polystyrène et pouvant contenir également un sel d'anion liposoluble, par exemple un borate de tétraphényle. Avec ce film, on obtient une électrode à membrane sélective permettant de déterminer rapidement de manière hautement sensible et hautement sélective des ions de carbonate d'hydrogène contenus dans un liquide organique, cette électrode étant de longue durée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>